# Astryx pages

Before placing any `@astryxdesign/core` component, open its page and follow it. The page is the spec.

- Docs: `https://astryx.atmeta.com/components/<Name>`. Each page has a Do list, a Don't list, and example code. Use those. Do not invent a prop, a layout, or a visual treatment the page does not show.
- Library source to read: [facebook/astryx](https://github.com/facebook/astryx). Do and Don't live in `packages/core/src/<Component>/<Component>.doc.mjs` (`guidance: true` is Do, `guidance: false` is Don't). Examples live in `apps/storybook/stories/`. Do not treat that repository's pull requests as this product's state.
- Product state: the latest pull request on [sdh2222/eth-tokyo](https://github.com/sdh2222/eth-tokyo/pulls). Read it before a screen change. The catalog and the last check are in `docs/design/astryx.md`.
